{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests adequate. I did not read any implementation source. I mapped each obligation in `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` to the tests below.\n\n**Combining and including every applicable contribution**\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` asserts the combined set for a requirement. It includes the subject declaration, cited declarations, terms, and current `{test}` items, and excludes distant requirements, `{impl}` items and earlier evidence.\n- It also checks the example-subject case.\n- `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` checks which edge directions contribute. `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` check `:impl:` and `:test:` anchors, with exact input lists. `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` checks references found in docs and plain text. `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` checks the fixed exclusions on discovered references.\n- Other contribution kinds are covered by `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]`, `fn[book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance]` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`) and `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]`.\n\n**Deduplicating identical selections**\n- In `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]`, `:impl:` and `:test:` name the same file. The expected input list has that file once, which is an exact equality assertion.\n- In `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]`, the same requirement is cited twice, the same term is shared by two requirements, and the same built-in text is cited twice. Each appears exactly once, and the total is 5.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read]` checks that a delivered item is recorded once.\n\n**Reporting unresolvable inputs before inference**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request]` makes the subject's own declaration unreadable. It asserts a nonzero exit, that stderr names the path, that the model endpoint was never contacted, and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n- `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` covers a missing anchor file and an anchor naming a missing node.\n- `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]` shows that stale earlier inputs are not treated as mandatory.\n\n**Supplying the complete set in the initial request**\n- `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` parses the \"Mandatory inputs\" block of the first request and checks its contents. It also checks that `prepared_inputs` equals the initial inputs plus later deliveries.\n- The citation and site prompt tests (`fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]` and the site test) check that the initial prompt carries the complete mandatory set.\n- `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` checks the prompt contains the selected node's source and not its siblings.\n\n**Visibility under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider` and denial abort under `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`**\n- `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` ignores the declaration file and expects `PermissionDenied` naming the path.\n- `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` checks an ignored evidence directory and a symlink alias.\n- `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` checks an ignored anchored file.\n- The citation test checks an ignored term file.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` shows untracked files are visible.\n- The full abort semantics (no evidence written, usage record, batch behaviour) belong to `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`'s own tests and are not reassessed here.\n\nThe clause requiring contributing requirements to cite this requirement and define their contributions is a drafting rule for those requirements. Their own text carries it out. It needs no test here.\n\nI found no gap and no marking gap.",
  "references": "528817a22486111257e77556ddd138b2ff22971a54040b26e8cb63bd67df9961",
  "inputs": [
